  {
   "n": 9,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>With increase in temperature, which of the following statement(s) regarding viscosity is/are CORRECT?<br />\n </p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "the dynamic viscosity of a gas increases"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "the dynamic viscosity of a liquid decreases"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "the kinematic viscosity of a gas increases"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "the kinematic viscosity of a liquid increases"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, B, C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a, b, c)<br />\n&bull; With increase in temperature cohesive forces between the liquid molecules decreases resulting in decrease in viscosity of liquids.<br />\n&bull; With increase in temperature molecular collisions between the molecules of gases increases resulting in increase in viscosity of gases.<br />\n&bull; Kinematic viscosity of liquid may increase or decrease.</p>"
  },
